hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18092","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Adi ibn Thabit from Zayd ibn Wahb narrating from Thabit son of Wadiah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a man brought him lizards he had hunted, then he kept looking at a lizard thereof, then he said: A nation was transformed, so I do not know, perhaps this is of them."
"18093","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Adi ibn Thabit informed me, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Wahb narrating from Thabit son of Wadiah, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with lizards he had hunted, he said: Then he kept looking at it and turning it, and he said: A nation was transformed, so it is not known what it did, and I do not know, perhaps this is of them."
"18094","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Adi ibn Thabit from Zayd ibn Wahb from Thabit son of Wadiah that a man from Banu Fazarah brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lizards, he said: Then he kept turning a lizard thereof before him and said: A nation was transformed. He said: And most of my knowledge that he said: I do not know, perhaps this is of them."
"18095","Shubah said: And Husayn from Zayd ibn Wahb from Hudhayfah said: Then he mentioned something like this. He said: Then he neither ordered him nor forbade anyone from it."
"18096","Husayn narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us from Husayn from Zayd ibn Wahb al-Juhani from Thabit ibn Yazid son of Wadaah al-Ansari, he said: We hunted lizards while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in one of his expeditions, he said: Then the people cooked and grilled, he said: Then I took a lizard and grilled it, then I brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and placed it before him, then he took a stick and kept turning with it his fingers, or counting them, then he said: A nation from Banu Israil was transformed to beasts in the earth, and I do not know which beasts they are. He said: I said: The people have grilled. He said: Then he did not eat of it, nor did he forbid them from it."
"18097","Affan and Muhammad ibn Jafar both said: Shubah narrated to us, Affan in his hadith said: al-Hakam informed me from Zayd ibn Wahb from al-Bara ibn Azib from Thabit son of Wadiah, he said: He brought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a lizard, then he said: A transformed nation, and Allah knows best. Affan said: And Allah knows best."
